Implementing a multi-tree list (also known as a hierarchical tree) within an Angular application involves several steps, including setting up the basic structure of your component and integrating it with the Angular Material library for TreeList functionality.

Here's a step-by-step guide to help you get started:

### 1. Set Up Your Project

First, make sure you have Node.js installed on your machine. Then create a new Angular project using `ng new` or any other way you prefer.

```bash
ng new my-multi-tree-list-app
cd my-multi-tree-list-app
```

### 2. Install Required Packages

You will need to install Angular Material and some utilities for handling trees.

```bash
npm install @angular/material @agm/core
```

Additionally, you might want to use a library like `@ag-grid/angular` if you're looking for more advanced tree functionalities.

### 3. Create the Multi-Tree List Component

Create a new component that will serve as the container for your multi-tree list.

#### `src/app/multi-tree-list/multi-tree-list.component.ts`

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { MatTreeModule } from '@angular/material/tree';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-multi-tree-list',
  templateUrl: './multi-tree-list.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./multi-tree-list.component.css']
})
export class MultiTreeListComponent {
  treeData: Array<{ id: string; label: string; children?: Array<{ id: string; label: string }> }> = [
    { id: '1', label: 'Root' },
    {
      id: '2',
      label: 'Child 1',
      children: [
        { id: '2a', label: 'Grandchild 1' },
        { id: '2b', label: 'Grandchild 2' }
      ]
    },
    { id: '3', label: 'Child 2' }
  ];

  nodes: Array<MatTreeNodeModel> = [];

  constructor() {}

  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.populateNodes(this.treeData);
  }

  populateNodes(treeData: Array<{ id: string; label: string; children?: Array<{ id: string; label: string }> }>, parent?: MatTreeNodeModel): void {
    if (!parent) {
      parent = this.nodes[0];
    }

    for (let item of treeData) {
      const node = new MatTreeNodeModel();
      node.id = item.id;
      node.label = item.label;
      node.parentId = parent.id;

      // Add child nodes recursively
      this.populateNodes(item.children || [], node);

      // Add the current node to the data array
      parent.children.push(node);
    }
  }
}
```

